UFS storage driver for the Google Pixel 7

The driver 'exynos_ufs' is a port of the UFS and SCSI cores of Linux with
the vendor's Exynos UFS host-controller driver. It provides the logical
units of the storage (sda, sdb, ...) as Block sessions with the block size
of the unit (4 KiB), and reports them if configured with 'report: yes'.
The driver does not handle partitions. The inline encryption of the vendor's
driver is not built. It needs the ports 'pixel_linux' and 'google_soc_gs'.

Block sessions are assigned to units by policies, e.g.:

! + config | report: yes
!   + default-policy | device: sda | writeable: no

The scenario 'run/exynos_ufs_pixel' reads the first 256 MiB of 'sda' via
'block_tester' without writing to the storage:

! make run/exynos_ufs_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
